>> title: Roasted Sweet Potatoes
>> category: Vegetables & Sides
>> tags: sweet potato, roast, sheet pan, side, bowl
>> counters: The Bowl Shop
>> aka: roasted sweet potato, sweet potato wedges, roast kumara, caramelised sweet potatoes, sweet potato half-moons, garlic roasted sweet potatoes
>> pairs-with: rice-pilaf, tahini-sauce
>> servings: 4
>> time: 45 min
>> step.1: The pan goes into the oven empty and comes out at 450°F. It all happens in the first thirty seconds.
>> step.2: toss in oil and salt
>> step.3: roast 450°F (230°C) 20 min, cut face down, not moved
>> step.4: turn and finish 10 min
>> step.5: stir the maple-lime glaze
>> step.6: toss on the hot pan

The pan goes in the oven empty and comes out at 450°F. Everything good about this happens in the first thirty seconds, on hot metal, and nothing you do later gets it back.

Toss @sweet potatoes{2%lb}(900 g; scrubbed, unpeeled, in 3/4-in half-moons) with @olive oil{2%Tbs}(30 mL) and @kosher salt{1%tsp} until every cut face is wet. Half-moons rather than cubes, because a cube has six small faces and a half-moon has one big one, and the flat face is the entire recipe.

Lay @&(~1)oiled sweet potatoes{} cut face down on the #sheet pan{} you preheated and ~roast{20%min} at 450°F (230°C) **without opening the door**. Sweet potato is about six percent sugar, so the face that is touching metal caramelises rather than browning; lift a piece to look at twelve minutes and you trade the crust for steam. Oil the pan, do not line it — parchment insulates and foil sticks to the sugar.

Turn @&(~1)roasted sweet potatoes{} with a thin metal spatula, scraping rather than lifting, and ~roast{10%min} more, until the second side gives and the edges have gone almost black.

Stir @maple syrup{1%Tbs}(15 mL), @lime juice{1%Tbs}(15 mL), @red chile flakes{1/2%tsp} and @flaky salt{1/2%tsp} together in a small bowl.

Toss @&(~2)roasted sweet potatoes{} with @&(~1)maple-lime glaze{} on the hot pan, off the heat, and let it hiss down for a minute. The glaze goes on at the end for the same reason the salt went on at the start: a tablespoon of maple syrup put on at minute one is thirty minutes from burnt sugar, and there is nothing between glazed and bitter.
